Z||000000||SloPonti||02-07-2000||07:48 PM||||here is a picture of the box that i remove that is behing the side scoop! this box is really restrictive! i removed it and am now making a custom tube for the air cleaner hose to fit onto! why was this box there and has anyone removed it already! how was the perfomance afterwards compared to having it on there!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/box.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/sloponti/box.jpg</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Capt Fiero||02-07-2000||08:27 PM||||This box realy has me confussed, I have on more than one ocassion droped something down into the center of the aircleaner, all I did to get it out was remove the outside grill and there it was, does this mean that the water seperator is off of my car already.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||02-08-2000||02:08 AM||||The box is there to keep water and large objects from getting sucked in.  Pontiac did an excellent job on the design of it, it's not restrictive at all.  I have not read about an actual improvement in power by removing it.  The only difference I've read about is if you remove it you can hear how much your engine "sucks"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  intake howl.<P>If you get rid of the air cleaner assembley and stick a cone filter on the end of that custom tube, you <B>might</B> see some improvement.  Couldn't tell you how much, tho.  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000003||SloPonti||02-08-2000||01:31 PM||||i think i will try it with it off and see what happens! will let you know the outcome!<BR>thanks <BR>Rob||||reg||10
Z||000004||1FST2M6||02-08-2000||01:53 PM||||You may have read that this piece has no bearing on engine performance. But what others have failed to take into account while testing is the air speed and air pressure on the body of the vehicle. After taking this in to account I have noted not only a noticeable horsepower increase but also a measurable one. After taking air pressure measurements while driving the car and then reproducing the same atmospheric conditions in the intake system. The results showed an 9hp increase at 44mph in 2nd gear and almost 14 lbft of torque. And that’s just one gear! Shown on a Dynojet Chassis Dyno model 248. I'll go to the shop and print our Dyno results and how we did it... I'll make sure and post it up here too SOON!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Capt Fiero||02-08-2000||03:05 PM||||Yes yes yes, DYNO results please.  I am working on a little gadget to test, air filters, holly style scoops and such in a real world envoirment, I am makeing a new air tube that goes between the air box and the plennium, this new tube will not have the rear valve cover breather tube attatched, it is going to have a Vaccume guage hooked to it with a line that goes into the cockpit of the car.  I will be able to run the car without an airfilter and the stock outside air grill, assumming GM did a good job I should get a reading of zero vaccume, meaning that the air is flowing smoothly, I then can further test my theory by installing the dirtyest air filter that I can and then drive the car foot to the floor on the freeway, I should get a reading of 1 - 1.5lbs Vacume meaning that the engine is having a hard time sucking the air.  OK that should give me a base line, then install various brands of Air Filters, side scoops and run with and without the water seperator and well the results should be interesting if nothing else.  If anybody would like to help with testing feel free, I am in Surrey B.C. Canada, 604-507-7754.<BR>David||||reg||1
Z||000006||87PegasusGT||02-08-2000||03:43 PM||||I have also removed the baffle and substituted an (I think 3 1/2 )aluminum airduct pipe (turnable joint)for acouple bucks from Office Depot. Definitely sounds cool and yes, I can feel the difference especially at higher speeds and rpms.||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||02-08-2000||10:11 PM||||As a watertrap this box is absolutely useless. The "hump" would go down not up. GM makes a practice of having intake mufflers to quiet the hissing of the intake. When I took mine off of my 4 cyl and added a pipe that I had bought from Home Depot for 2 dollars and used the generic holley type scoop I took off .3 off of my best 1/4 mile times. I have done this with the V6 but I did it while the engine was being built so I don't know how it was before. <BR>9 horsepower though? I would have to be skeptical but who can argue with a dyno. Was that "adjusted" or at the wheel? I have always relied on wheel (real) dyno readings. No matter the source, Ive never really trusted "adjusted dyno reading at the flywheel." It would be interesting to see the entire graph and see if the curve has shifted down to lower end torque. <BR>There is probably a little truth behind Ram Air...<P>Congratulations 2M6! You are about to bust open and finally answer a small disagreement that we have been having at the shop for years!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 02-08-2000).]||||reg||1
